WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:13.234
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:14.297 --> 00:00:17.908
Man, I don't get why that guy
didn't just run out of the room.

00:00:17.908 --> 00:00:20.832
I guess he thinks he's bad ass
enough to take on the aliens

00:00:20.832 --> 00:00:22.655
without the use of weapons.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.901
That seems kind of stupid to me.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.267
[glass shatters]
WHOA! Th...

00:00:28.954 --> 00:00:31.882
Okay, first thing's first.
Did anything follow me?

00:00:31.882 --> 00:00:33.124
No?

00:00:33.124 --> 00:00:36.637
So, what the fuck is this? This
is what "containment" looks like?

00:00:36.637 --> 00:00:39.225
Or, was he just carrying a
grenade and... tripped?

00:00:39.225 --> 00:00:40.199
[vortigese]

00:00:40.199 --> 00:00:41.615
Yeah, I can hear them!
[vortigese]

00:00:41.615 --> 00:00:42.868
THEY'RE ALREADY HERE!

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.998
Wow! This thing works great!

00:00:47.998 --> 00:00:49.786
I don't know why the
inventor didn't want it.

00:00:49.786 --> 00:00:51.750
[teleportation sound, vortigese]

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.701
What was that?

00:00:54.045 --> 00:00:54.968
Ah hah!

00:00:56.572 --> 00:00:57.267
[shudders]

00:00:59.766 --> 00:01:00.300
Jesus...!

00:01:04.256 --> 00:01:05.430
Okay...

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:11.635
So, I think what we can conclude here is
blue energy is superior to green energy.

00:01:11.635 --> 00:01:14.636
And bees, but that was
already one of our assumptions.

00:01:14.636 --> 00:01:15.297
Wuh-hoah!

00:01:15.297 --> 00:01:17.291
GUARD: Sir?
I could've fried you,

00:01:17.291 --> 00:01:19.975
but you're wearing blue so I
guess that's a sign.

00:01:19.975 --> 00:01:22.553
Hey, you don't--yeah, I'm just
going to take this.

00:01:22.553 --> 00:01:25.961
I mean, I don't see you trying
to stop me and I need that ammo.

00:01:25.961 --> 00:01:28.835
GUARD: I'd like to get my hands
on the guy responsible for THIS mess.

00:01:28.835 --> 00:01:30.791
Well, that's a complicated question.

00:01:30.791 --> 00:01:33.499
I think Black Mesa has evolved
as a group consciousness

00:01:33.499 --> 00:01:36.857
so that no individual truly
knows what he's doing.

00:01:36.857 --> 00:01:38.042
Like this guy.

00:01:38.042 --> 00:01:39.054
SCIENTIST: Freeman, isn't it?

00:01:39.054 --> 00:01:39.925
Recognize!

00:01:39.925 --> 00:01:41.280
SCIENTIST: You'll need to
activate both pumps

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.856
What? No!
SCIENTIST: to flood the reactor.

00:01:42.856 --> 00:01:45.856
SCIENTIST: And then that the access pipe
down there will take you to the core.

00:01:45.856 --> 00:01:46.209
No!

00:01:46.209 --> 00:01:47.061
SCIENTIST: Time is short!

00:01:47.061 --> 00:01:48.841
I'm not the maintenance man!

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:50.698
You have bad information!

00:01:50.698 --> 00:01:55.152
And what reactor? Is this it?
The one with the big crack in it?

00:01:55.152 --> 00:01:57.642
We're not on the same page here.
Look at me.

00:01:57.642 --> 00:02:00.710
Actually, hold up, I'll take this
stuff off your hands for you.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:04.507
Okay, so you just stay here and keep
staring at the wall. You're good at that.

00:02:04.507 --> 00:02:06.574
[announcement klaxon]

00:02:06.574 --> 00:02:11.614
PA: Biological force detected in
primary coolant system.

00:02:11.614 --> 00:02:14.553
Biological force in the coolant system.

00:02:14.553 --> 00:02:17.759
Well, there's the problem. An alien
must've teleported inside it.

00:02:17.759 --> 00:02:20.419
GUARD: All that target range
time is going to pay off today!

00:02:20.419 --> 00:02:22.205
Even down a magazine, huh?

00:02:22.205 --> 00:02:26.866
Hey, I didn't notice that blood
stain before, Mr. Target Range.

00:02:26.866 --> 00:02:30.200
Yeah, the splatter looks
like it came from here.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.730
Holy shit! You shot
somebody, didn't you?!

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:35.573
I guess you're not a pushover;
that's not alien blood!

00:02:35.573 --> 00:02:38.359
GUARD: I don't know if we should go
any further, th-this doesn't look right.

00:02:38.359 --> 00:02:41.723
Yeah, I BET you don't me looking
any further into this!

00:02:41.723 --> 00:02:43.926
But if you shot him, where's the body?

00:02:43.926 --> 00:02:45.312
Oh, there he is!

00:02:45.312 --> 00:02:46.383
So, you killed him.

00:02:46.383 --> 00:02:48.724
Those aliens were just feeding on him.

00:02:48.724 --> 00:02:50.564
Yeah, he's not even armed.

00:02:50.564 --> 00:02:53.891
Wow, I'm going to watch
my back around here!

00:02:53.891 --> 00:02:57.381
I don't want any surprises from
Captain Trigger Finger over there.

00:02:57.381 --> 00:03:01.528
I mean, the other people who shot
at me, I mostly knew it was coming,

00:03:01.528 --> 00:03:03.936
but this... shit!

00:03:03.936 --> 00:03:07.367
Civilization's falling
apart pretty fast!

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:11.418
I mean, that's kind of scary, shooting
the scientist. I'm a scientist.

00:03:11.418 --> 00:03:13.988
The guards aren't on our side,
they're on their side!

00:03:13.988 --> 00:03:15.267
[metal groaning, rumbling]

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.072
Oh god!
[metal groaning, rumbling]

00:03:16.072 --> 00:03:17.708
[metal groaning, rumbling]

00:03:17.708 --> 00:03:21.267
This place is dangerous. And
nobody knows what they're doing.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.910
There's probably going to be a
Congressional hearing about us later

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:26.096
asking, "How did this happen?"

00:03:26.096 --> 00:03:32.154
And every single person is going
to say, "Uhhh... uhhh... uh..."

00:03:32.154 --> 00:03:34.624
Okay, did that guard
shoot these guys, too?!

00:03:34.624 --> 00:03:36.418
Do they have any bullet holes in them?

00:03:36.418 --> 00:03:37.679
Actually, I don't want to know.

00:03:37.679 --> 00:03:40.962
Some people thrive in chaos
a little too much.

00:03:40.962 --> 00:03:44.482
Everyone else sees disaster, he
sees a human shooting gallery.

00:03:44.482 --> 00:03:45.767
[teleportation sound]
Oh no!

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:51.664
Yeah, what, you're going to
cover up for him?!

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:54.388
I dunno. I've killed people, too!

00:03:54.388 --> 00:03:58.613
But, the difference is I didn't kill
them BECAUSE they were alive.

00:03:58.613 --> 00:04:00.481
I needed a reason...?

00:04:00.481 --> 00:04:01.100
Daah!

00:04:07.063 --> 00:04:08.586
Shhh...

00:04:08.586 --> 00:04:11.257
I really like how the--
whoa, what was that?!

00:04:11.257 --> 00:04:13.038
Somebody's up there!

00:04:13.038 --> 00:04:17.025
I am SO certain I am not
hallucinating this time.

00:04:17.025 --> 00:04:19.598
And I have a gun! I can prove it!

00:04:19.598 --> 00:04:20.113
See?

00:04:21.049 --> 00:04:22.567
SHIT! I'm spent!

00:04:24.188 --> 00:04:25.922
PA: ...main reactor core...

00:04:25.922 --> 00:04:28.868
Quit complaining about the reactor!
I found the contaminant!

00:04:31.327 --> 00:04:34.010
Is he running from me?
This one has brains!

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:35.940
We can solve that problem.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.214
[agrunt grumbles]
Shut up!

00:04:37.214 --> 00:04:38.609
[explosion]

00:04:38.609 --> 00:04:40.784
I wonder if he was filming me.

00:04:40.784 --> 00:04:43.505
Well, I'm taking off this plasma pack.

00:04:43.505 --> 00:04:48.255
It's amazing but I need to fire
it for MORE than 10 seconds total.

00:04:48.255 --> 00:04:50.849
Gragh... that's better.

00:04:50.849 --> 00:04:56.448
Yeah, it's a prototype. It only lasts for
10 seconds and weighs at least 50 pounds,

00:04:56.448 --> 00:04:59.308
but, MAN, it makes things explode.

00:04:59.308 --> 00:05:02.777
We could've sold it to the military
without any further improvements.

00:05:02.777 --> 00:05:06.665
I especially I liked how the aliens
I hit with it became totally stunned

00:05:06.665 --> 00:05:10.223
with this "Oh, my shit is
getting wrecked" face.

00:05:10.223 --> 00:05:12.133
Okay, any surprises?

00:05:13.231 --> 00:05:14.153
No.

00:05:14.153 --> 00:05:15.312
[metal groaning, rumbling]

00:05:15.312 --> 00:05:16.541
Oh, dammit!
[metal groaning, rumbling]

00:05:16.541 --> 00:05:17.734
[metal groaning, rumbling]

00:05:18.837 --> 00:05:22.418
I still think some of the aliens
are teleporting inside the walls.

00:05:22.418 --> 00:05:23.106
PA: Danger...

00:05:23.106 --> 00:05:23.567
Danger!

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:29.230
PA: ...detected in Radioactive
Materials Handling Bay.

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:30.634
[telportation sound]
Shit.

00:05:34.346 --> 00:05:35.467
OH MY GOD!

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.284
OH MY GOD!

00:05:37.284 --> 00:05:38.997
OOOOOOOOOOH!

00:05:38.997 --> 00:05:41.560
That one almost went inside me!

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:43.048
Aaaah...

00:05:43.048 --> 00:05:44.934
PA: Cross-dimensional power

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:47.607
What?!
PA: field activity detected.

00:05:47.607 --> 00:05:51.033
Cross-dimensional pow--no, wait.
What is this?

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:55.531
Okay. "No access." I believe them!

00:05:55.531 --> 00:05:57.448
So... Oh, a switch.

00:05:57.448 --> 00:06:00.291
Maybe this will fix... everything.

00:06:00.291 --> 00:06:01.868
[telportation sound]
NO!

00:06:03.252 --> 00:06:04.767
IS THAT WHAT THIS SWITCH DOES?!

00:06:05.728 --> 00:06:06.400
Christ!

00:06:07.963 --> 00:06:10.184
Okay, one more, I'm shutting it off!

00:06:10.184 --> 00:06:14.033
I didn't know this was a monster
generator, that's a terrible idea!

00:06:14.776 --> 00:06:16.689
Oh, this is just a pump.

00:06:16.689 --> 00:06:20.247
I guess this is all just a
terrifying coincidence.

00:06:20.247 --> 00:06:22.456
Jesus, I'm getting low on bullets.

00:06:22.456 --> 00:06:24.713
I have one spare mag then I'm out.

00:06:24.713 --> 00:06:27.527
The scientists probably don't
keep any spares on them.

00:06:27.527 --> 00:06:30.214
PA: ...reports dimensional
contamination.

00:06:30.214 --> 00:06:33.398
Dimensional contamination.
There we go again.

00:06:33.398 --> 00:06:37.085
Whoever set up this intercom
system clearly wanted to fight me.

00:06:37.085 --> 00:06:40.560
I keep hearing "dimensional power",
"dimensional contamination",

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.616
what the fuck are they talking about?!

00:06:42.616 --> 00:06:46.324
I'm pretty sure these aliens are
three-dimensional!

00:06:46.324 --> 00:06:51.614
Probably from somewhere deep in
space, but space isn't another dimension!

00:06:51.614 --> 00:06:54.710
Does somebody here think they're
Buckaroo Banzai?!

00:06:54.710 --> 00:07:00.182
But, okay, let's say that teleportation event
represents cross-dimensional activity.

00:07:00.182 --> 00:07:01.655
How do we know this?

00:07:01.655 --> 00:07:05.531
Have we figured all this out in
the past two days during a panic?

00:07:05.531 --> 00:07:09.994
And, invented and set up cross-dimensional
detectors around the facility

00:07:09.994 --> 00:07:11.588
like they're smoke alarms

00:07:11.588 --> 00:07:16.349
AND set up a network-to-intercom
system to inform us when one happens?

00:07:16.349 --> 00:07:20.181
If so, WOW! Color me impressed!

00:07:20.181 --> 00:07:22.875
That's pretty good considering
your reactor is down

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:24.558
and you have a rogue security guard

00:07:24.558 --> 00:07:27.367
dancing through the halls and
shooting your science team.

00:07:27.367 --> 00:07:30.760
I wouldn't be able to get work
done under those conditions.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:34.795
Silly me, I thought it was turning
into Lord of the Flies around here.

00:07:34.795 --> 00:07:38.463
Okay, I've already been here...
Yeah, I guess this way.

00:07:38.463 --> 00:07:42.358
But, yeah, these announcements
aren't fooling me. We're on the brink.

00:07:42.358 --> 00:07:44.786
I bet if I wait a few hours and
then come back,

00:07:44.786 --> 00:07:47.842
that security guard will be wearing
a necklace made out of ears

00:07:47.842 --> 00:07:52.296
and painting pictures of demons or some crap
on the walls with the scientists' blood.

00:07:52.296 --> 00:07:53.499
And then he's going to take--

00:07:53.499 --> 00:07:55.499
[explosion]

00:07:55.499 --> 00:07:58.007
[growls]

00:07:58.007 --> 00:07:59.067
Well...

00:08:00.144 --> 00:08:01.701
Shit...

00:08:05.001 --> 00:08:07.968
Y'know, all this concrete dust
is a breathing hazard.

